{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HtmKqzeVXTpLWrnRG3d5fa","type":"tool_result","content":"340\t\n341\t/// Hooks the TLS layer invokes on the application.  One trait\n342\t/// covers ALPN selection, the resumption-ticket store, and\n343\t/// certificate verification.  Default implementations cover\n344\t/// the simple cases; override for custom behavior.\n345\t///\n346\t/// The application installs an implementation at QUIC-context\n347\t/// construction time (one entry point — no C-style global\n348\t/// registry of function pointers).\n349\tpub trait TlsCallbacks: Send {\n350\t    /// Negotiate ALPN from the client's proposal list.  Default:\n351\t    /// pick the first proposal that matches the server's\n352\t    /// configured ALPN list (set on the backend's config).\n353\t    fn select_alpn(&mut self, _list: &[&[u8]]) -> Option<usize> {\n354\t        None\n355\t    }\n356\t\n357\t    /// Server-side: look up a previously-issued session ticket\n358\t    /// keyed by the SNI / ALPN combination.  Default: return\n359\t    /// `None` (no resumption).\n360\t    fn lookup_ticket(&mut self, _sni: &str, _alpn: &str) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\n361\t        None\n362\t    }\n363\t\n364\t    /// Server-side: persist a freshly-issued session ticket.\n365\t    /// Default: discard.\n366\t    fn store_ticket(&mut self, _sni: &str, _alpn: &str, _ticket: &[u8]) {}\n367\t\n368\t    /// Verify the peer certificate chain.  Default: trust any\n369\t    /// chain rooted in the system trust store (backends that\n370\t    /// don't have a system store provide their own default).\n371\t    fn verify_certificate(&mut self, _certs: &[&[u8]]) -> Result<(), Error> {\n372\t        Ok(())\n373\t    }\n374\t}\n375\t\n376\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n377\t// Backend-construction errors.\n378\t\n379\t/// Backend-construction failure (bad config, unsupported\n380\t/// version, etc.).  Distinct from the runtime-error\n381\t/// [`crate::Error`] so type-system can enforce that\n382\t/// `start_session` doesn't return a generic `Error`.\n383\t#[derive(Debug)]\n384\tpub struct ConfigError {\n385\t    pub message: alloc::string::String,\n386\t}\n387\t\n388\t#[cfg(test)]\n389\tmod test {}\n390\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c078a458-8d27-4b1b-b12a-e775d28f8c36","uuid":"bd4dd165-76ef-405d-80f0-9bcacacd6732","timestamp":"2026-05-07T09:34:49.746Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/tls.rs","content":"\n/// Hooks the TLS layer invokes on the application.  One trait\n/// covers ALPN selection, the resumption-ticket store, and\n/// certificate verification.  Default implementations cover\n/// the simple cases; override for custom behavior.\n///\n/// The application installs an implementation at QUIC-context\n/// construction time (one entry point — no C-style global\n/// registry of function pointers).\npub trait TlsCallbacks: Send {\n    /// Negotiate ALPN from the client's proposal list.  Default:\n    /// pick the first proposal that matches the server's\n    /// configured ALPN list (set on the backend's config).\n    fn select_alpn(&mut self, _list: &[&[u8]]) -> Option<usize> {\n        None\n    }\n\n    /// Server-side: look up a previously-issued session ticket\n    /// keyed by the SNI / ALPN combination.  Default: return\n    /// `None` (no resumption).\n    fn lookup_ticket(&mut self, _sni: &str, _alpn: &str) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\n        None\n    }\n\n    /// Server-side: persist a freshly-issued session ticket.\n    /// Default: discard.\n    fn store_ticket(&mut self, _sni: &str, _alpn: &str, _ticket: &[u8]) {}\n\n    /// Verify the peer certificate chain.  Default: trust any\n    /// chain rooted in the system trust store (backends that\n    /// don't have a system store provide their own default).\n    fn verify_certificate(&mut self, _certs: &[&[u8]]) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        Ok(())